  "Attributes": [
    {
      "Id": 759635,
      "attributeType": "LongString",
      "attributeName": "AIDescription",
      "attributeRelationType": "None",
      "Value": "## 141 Chip Monitor (Commodore 64) - Description\n\n141 Chip Monitor is a quirky and unique simulation game for the Commodore 64, placing you in the role of a technician responsible for monitoring the vital signs of a giant, sentient computer chip named Chip. Developed by Mastertronic, the game blends elements of simulation, puzzle-solving, and a surprisingly charming narrative.\n\nChip, the titular character, is experiencing a series of malfunctions, and it's your job to diagnose and rectify them before he completely shuts down. You navigate a series of interconnected screens, each representing a different system within Chip's complex internal structure. Using a variety of diagnostic tools and by carefully observing fluctuating readings, you must identify the source of the problems – from overheating to data corruption. \n\nThe gameplay involves adjusting parameters, rerouting power, and even performing virtual surgery on Chip’s circuits. Success depends on quick thinking and a keen eye for detail. With its distinctive pixel art, catchy chiptune soundtrack, and humorous storyline, 141 Chip Monitor offers a genuinely original and entertaining experience on the Commodore 64."
    },
